sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Metered inference: an MPP session on Tempo with vouchers, a top-up and a cooperative close
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: Metered inference: an MPP session on Tempo with vouchers, a top-up and a cooperative close. 3 participants: Client agent, Inference API server, and Tempo channel escrow (TIP-20 precompile in v2). 13 steps, 10 crossing a trust boundary, 9 failure branches. Based on several protocols MPP core draft-httpauth-payment-01 Tempo session draft-tempo-session-00 (v2 text merged 2026-06-25) (2026-06-25). Step 1: Client agent to Inference API server: POST /v1/chat/completions with Accept-Payment. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 2: Inference API server to Client agent: 402 with WWW-Authenticate: Payment, method tempo, intent session. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 3: Client agent to Client agent: Choose a deposit, sign the open transaction and a zero voucher. Step 4: Client agent to Inference API server: Retry with Authorization: Payment, action open. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The challenge id is unknown, used or expired: 402 with a fresh challenge and a matching problem type such as invalid-challenge or payment-expired. Step 5: Inference API server to Tempo channel escrow (TIP-20 precompile in v2): Broadcast the open transaction. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 6: Inference API server to Client agent: 200, stream starts, Payment-Receipt in headers. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 7: Client agent to Inference API server: Voucher per unit batch (action voucher, HEAD allowed). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The voucher total exceeds the deposit: Rejected (session/amount-exceeds-deposit). If The increase is below minVoucherDelta: Rejected (session/delta-too-small). If The voucher is signed by the wrong key: Rejected (session/signer-mismatch). Step 8: Inference API server to Client agent: SSE event payment-need-voucher. If No voucher arrives within the server's timeout (for example 60 seconds): The server should close the stream the agent has paid only for what its vouchers covered. Step 9: Client agent to Inference API server: Top up (action topUp). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The challenge id is unknown or expired: Rejected with problem type challenge-not-found. Step 10: Inference API server to Tempo channel escrow (TIP-20 precompile in v2): Broadcast topUp settle when the server chooses. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 11: Client agent to Inference API server: Close (action close) with the final voucher. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 12: Inference API server to Tempo channel escrow (TIP-20 precompile in v2): close: capture max(spent, settled), refund the rest. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The server never closes (forced close): The agent calls requestClose on chain a grace period of at least 15 minutes starts in which the server can still settle or close the spec advises waiting at least 16 minutes before withdraw, which returns all unsettled funds. If The agent tops up while a close request is pending: The topUp cancels the close request and emits CloseRequestCancelled. If A close voucher equal to the settled amount (mppx before 0.4.11, CVE-2026-34209): The vulnerable server accepted it, letting anyone close or grief a channel for free fixed in 0.4.11. Step 13: Inference API server to Client agent: Final receipt with txHash (SSE payment-receipt event).
  autonumber
  participant p_client as Client agent
  participant p_server as Inference API server
  participant p_escrow as Tempo channel escrow (TIP-20 precompile in v2)
  p_client->>p_server: POST /v1/chat/completions with Accept-Payment
  Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_server-->>p_client: 402 with WWW-Authenticate: Payment, method tempo, intent session
  Note over p_server,p_client: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_client->>p_client: Choose a deposit, sign the open transaction and a zero voucher
  alt Expected path
    p_client->>p_server: Retry with Authorization: Payment, action open
    Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The challenge id is unknown, used or expired
    Note over p_client,p_server: 402 with a fresh challenge and a matching problem type such as invalid-challenge or payment-expired.
  end
  p_server->>p_escrow: Broadcast the open transaction
  Note over p_server,p_escrow: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_server-->>p_client: 200, stream starts, Payment-Receipt in headers
  Note over p_server,p_client: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_client->>p_server: Voucher per unit batch (action voucher, HEAD allowed)
    Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The voucher total exceeds the deposit
    Note over p_client,p_server: Rejected (session/amount-exceeds-deposit).
  else The increase is below minVoucherDelta
    Note over p_client,p_server: Rejected (session/delta-too-small).
  else The voucher is signed by the wrong key
    Note over p_client,p_server: Rejected (session/signer-mismatch).
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_server-->>p_client: SSE event payment-need-voucher
  else No voucher arrives within the server#39;s timeout (for example 60 seconds)
    Note over p_server,p_client: The server should close the stream#59; the agent has paid only for what its vouchers covered.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_client->>p_server: Top up (action topUp)
    Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The challenge id is unknown or expired
    Note over p_client,p_server: Rejected with problem type challenge-not-found.
  end
  p_server->>p_escrow: Broadcast topUp#59; settle when the server chooses
  Note over p_server,p_escrow: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_client->>p_server: Close (action close) with the final voucher
  Note over p_client,p_server: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_server->>p_escrow: close: capture max(spent, settled), refund the rest
    Note over p_server,p_escrow: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The server never closes (forced close)
    Note over p_server,p_escrow: The agent calls requestClose on chain#59; a grace period of at least 15 minutes starts in which the server can still settle or close#59; the spec advises waiting at least 16 minutes before withdraw, which returns all unsettled funds.
  else The agent tops up while a close request is pending
    Note over p_server,p_escrow: The topUp cancels the close request and emits CloseRequestCancelled.
  else A close voucher equal to the settled amount (mppx before 0.4.11, CVE-2026-34209)
    Note over p_server,p_escrow: The vulnerable server accepted it, letting anyone close or grief a channel for free#59; fixed in 0.4.11.
  end
  p_server->>p_client: Final receipt with txHash (SSE payment-receipt event)
